joe_doufu schrieb:
> 
> I advanced my longsword skills and silver saber skills as much as I
> could; I figure I've got enough backup artifacts now I don't need to
> think about falling back on another weapon type.  First question: Is it
> useful for a knight to learn twoweapon?

Unless you really, really want to use a shield of reflection, yes. An
extra weapon gives a very nice chunk of extra damage and more than
compensates for the AC bonus of a shield.

> Assuming I had enchanted
> silversabers and longswords to choose from, which should I use as my
> secondary?

This depends on the primary weapon you use - in Gehennom, it's quite
nice to have one source of silver damage constantly equipped. If i
used Grayswandir as primary, i'd use a long sword as secondary, with
Excalibur (or Magicbane), i'd tend towards a silver sabre.

> Another question: I advanced my riding skill once because I could.  Was
> that a waste of a skill point?  My horses keep dying, is there anything
> other creature I could ride?  

Quadrupeds, dragons, jabberwocks, horses, unicorns, centaurs and a few
others are ridable. Ki-Rin are popular, but a bit difficult to keep
(they never eat and therefore can't recover tameness). Most
quadrupeds, all horses and unicorns are herbivores and will usually
starve to death fairly soon. 
Dragons are immensely popular, especially silver dragons, which can't
be disintegrated or death-rayed from under you. Yellow dragons are
petrification-resistant - cockatrices are less of a priority when
you're riding one of these.
Centaurs are somewhat interesting because they can use equipment, but
they won't get many hitpoints if you don't boost them with wraith
corpses and gain level potions.

> Questions about luckstones: I have about half a dozen now, some
> blessed.  Does it do me any good to have more than one at the same
> time? 

No. Blessed luckstones give the best effect, and 50 blessed luckstones
still give the same luck effect as a single one.

> Do they still work if they're in bags of holding?

No. Items with 'carried' effects like luckstones only work when
they're in your main inventory.

> Also, I have the "Orb of Fate" from that healer's bonespile, it's in a
> blessed bag of holding and I can't take it out so I have no way of
> testing if its cursed or safe.

It's not going to be safe. In order to even pick it up, you would have
to permanently convert to neutral, which is very definitely not
recommended (it will make the game unwinnable if you haven't been
admitted to the quest yet, and even after that, it'll cause a fair bit
of trouble and can put the game in an un-winnable state).

> Should I keep the bag with me or toss
> it by the wayside? 

You could stash it somewhere and consider later whether it's worth the
trouble of conversion; it's a pretty nice item, but it won't do you
any good in a bag.

